<title>GERMANY: Depfa H1 pretax profit up 23.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Depfa H1 pretax profit up 23.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    239.4  vs 212.7</p>
<p>    Group oper profit before provisions   314.4  vs 280.1</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit			218.9  vs 176.5</p>
<p>    Net interest income			 455    vs 412.6</p>
<p>    Net commission income		     63.8   vs 59.1</p>
<p>    Risk provisions			     75.0   vs 67.4*</p>
<p>    Administratuve costs			211.0  vs 193.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Deutsche Pfandbrief- und Hypothekenbank AG. The bank said in its interim report that it expected its DVFA earnings per share would be not below six marks per share for 1997.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
